# Integration Test Rules (Gherkin + Rest Assured)
- Feature files live in tests/integration/features/; step definitions in tests/integration/steps/.
- Write Gherkin in business language: Given a precondition, When an action, Then an observable outcome. No HTTP verbs or status codes in the Given/When/Then prose.
- One Scenario per behavior. Use Scenario Outline with an Examples table for data-driven cases, and source the rows from the test-data matrix.
- Keep assertions in step definitions, not in feature files.
- In Rest Assured steps, assert on status code and response body separately; assert the contract (fields, types), not just a 200.
- Centralize base URI, auth, and JSON (de)serialization in a shared request spec; do not rebuild the client per step.
- Tag scenarios (@discount, @smoke, @negative) so suites can be filtered in CI.
- Never hardcode environment URLs; read them from configuration.
